rules.requirement:
A landlord who serves a notice of termination for one of the following causes must pay relocation to the tenants:
- owner or relative move-in;
- demolition or permanent removal of the unit from housing use;
- temporary capital improvement work;
- substantial rehabilitation.

The amount is set per tenant and capped per unit. An additional amount is due for each elderly (60+) or disabled tenant, or for a household with minor children. Amounts adjust each March 1 and depend on the date the notice is served. Relocation for temporary capital improvement evictions of less than 20 days is governed by Cal. Civ. Code § 1947.9, not § 37.9C.
